{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>And one goat of purification-offering.</b> On all the days of the festival it is not written 'to make atonement for you,' because during the festival there are bullocks that come to make atonement for the nations, and therefore Scripture did not suspend the atonement upon Israel. Another interpretation: that which is not written in them 'to make atonement for you' is because they do not yet need atonement, as I explained in the perasha of Emor — and Yom HaKippurim makes atonement. A proof for the matter: from Yom HaKippurim onward, 'to make atonement for you' is not written."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:20:13.942127801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}